# macOS UI

Full notes: `docs/macos-client-patterns.md`.

- SwiftUI views describe UI only. Genealogy, SQLite, and identity stay in Go (FFI later).
- Keep `body` cheap and free of I/O. Put validation and actions on a model; inject a `GenealogyStore` protocol with a `FakeStore` for tests and previews.
- Prefer SwiftUI; wrap AppKit (panels, menus, `NSColor`) in small helpers.
- If a control will be UI-tested, give it a stable `.accessibilityIdentifier`.
- User-facing copy goes through typed `L10n` + String Catalogs. Follow `.cursor/skills/add-localized-string/SKILL.md`. Do not hard-code English in views/models.
- Put new screens under `macos/App/Features/<Feature>/` (view + model together). Reusable `PV*` chrome lives in `DesignSystem/` (see `macos/App/DesignSystem/README.md`). FFI/store types stay in `Platform/`. Do not add more files to a flat target root.
- UI layering (design system / recipes / snowflakes): [`.cursor/rules/design-system-layers.mdc`](design-system-layers.mdc). When adding or forking chrome, follow [`.cursor/skills/add-ui-component/SKILL.md`](../skills/add-ui-component/SKILL.md). When auditing an existing type for compose/refactor PRs, follow [`.cursor/skills/evaluate-ui-component/SKILL.md`](../skills/evaluate-ui-component/SKILL.md).
- Restoreable workspace places (sidebar destinations, deep pages, master–detail selection) go through `WorkspaceLocation` + `WorkspaceNavigation.go(to:)` (environment). Follow `.cursor/skills/add-workspace-location/SKILL.md`.
- Unit tests go in `macos/ProvenenciaTests/` (Swift Testing). Follow `.cursor/skills/add-swift-test/SKILL.md`. Do not co-locate `*Tests.swift` under `App/`.
